# Git and Version Control Rules
- You must always use the local Git CLI for version control tasks (e.g., checking status, staging, committing).
- Never use external GitHub MCP tools or look for custom API plugins for standard repository operations.
- Always check `git status` or `git diff` before committing to ensure only intended files are changed.
- Write clear, concise imperative-tone commit messages.
- DO NOT execute `git push` or `git remote` operations automatically unless explicitly requested by the user.
